lisa-design:
- privileges Check runs nothing as root (coordinator decision): kata-helper protocol as the owner (the helper is 0755), then `sudo -n -k -l <helper>` (listpw=any assumed: a user with a NOPASSWD rule may list without a password; -k ignores host init's cached login so a missing rule fails). The 0440 sudoers file's text is compared when readable, else its size. The owner comes from os/user, matches the regex, and isn't root; SUDO_USER is never read.
- Plan takes the sha256 of os.Executable(); Apply stages a copy 0700; root copies it into a root-owned temp dir, sha256sum -c, install -o root -g root -m 0755. The sudoers heredoc passes visudo -cf before install -m 0440.
- The helper's commands get exactly katahelper.Env (PATH, HOME=/root, NERDCTL_TOML=/dev/null), cwd /, a 1-minute timeout for list; list prints only workspace.ValidName names; usage exits 2, other failures 1 with one sanitised stderr line. main dispatches on argv[0] == kata-helper before anything else.
